    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711">

                <pb facs="1416" n="1404" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.70/5–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-07">May 7, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3592. This supersedes previous instructions.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d711-f1"/> You
                    are hereby authorized to sign agreement without amendment to Article XIV,
                    paragraph 9. You are, however, to make it clear to other signatories that this
                    Government interprets the term “Allied Commanders in Chief” to include not only
                    commanders designated by a combination of the powers named but also commanders
                    designated by any one of the powers. You may make this position a matter of
                    record by inserting the amended Article in the minutes of the Council
                    meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[The agreement for the Provisional European Inland Transport Organization was
                        signed at London on May 8, 1945. For text, see Department of State Executive
                        Agreement Series No. 458, or 59 Stat, (pt. 2) 1359. For a press statement
                        released on May 11, 1945, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bulletin</hi>, May 13, 1945, page 910.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d711-f1" n="45" xml:id="d711-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 3563, May 7, 1945, 11 a.m., to London, had authorized signature of the
                    Agreement subject to an amendment to article <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >xiv</hi>, paragraph 9 (840.70/4–3045).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
